{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Now HaShem will restore the splendor of Jacob like the splendor of Israel, when he is in his land. The meaning: He will restore them to their splendor, as Israel was of old in their splendor." "<b>In their emptiness</b> — The word is proof that the verb is intransitive, and so גפן בוקק is a verb and the intransitive subject is the fruit that corresponds to it; or it may be like the word שב (returning), found standing and going out. And the meaning of 'in their emptiness' — their desolation, like a blasted vine; therefore. [n: The Hebrew here is obscure; the grammatical argument about כי הפועל יוצא and the comparison to שב is compressed and possibly textually difficult. Rendered hyper-literally.]" "<b>And their tendrils</b> — like 'and they cut from there a tendril' (Numbers 13:23); [the word] returns to explain the spreading branches."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:34.916691929Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}